            <ArticleTitle>Variant angina complicated by polymorphic ventricular tachycardia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e47-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ijcard.2008.12.138</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of variant angina with a classic clinical presentation complicated by polymorphic ventricular tachycardia. The diagnosis was confirmed by demonstrating ST segment elevation during an episode of angina and subsequently by inducing multi-vessel coronary spasm with ergonovine. The patient was treated successfully with long-acting calcium-channel blockers and nitrates.</AbstractText>
